Subject: [PATCH 1/2] oss/freebsd-ports: Make ports without building deps
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: wrwvwvpynvyorrlrmzmvypqmnzzvplxz

Building a port in the ports tree installs each missing dependency by
building it from source first, which can take hours and changes the
host. To avoid that, ports work here has skipped the build and left it
to poudriere, so patches have gone out with their build and plist
unchecked.

port-make.sh builds the port alone. It first checks the port's direct
dependencies against the installed packages and, if any are missing,
lists them all with a pkg install line and exits 2 before make runs.
The operator installs them once and the build is retried. Only direct
dependencies are listed because pkg brings in their own run
dependencies, and their build dependencies are never needed.

STRICT_DEPENDS stays set while make runs, so a dependency the check
did not catch stops the build rather than being built. The work,
distfile, and options directories live under /var/tmp, since the
defaults are root-owned.
